# Generated by `npx cap sync ios`, and NOT safe to commit.
#
# The Capacitor CLI builds every dependency path in Package.swift with
# path.relative(), which emits BACKSLASHES when the sync runs on Windows. Those
# land inside Swift string literals, where \. \@ \h are invalid escapes and
# \node_modules contains a literal newline, so the manifest does not parse and
# Xcode cannot resolve packages. That is exactly what was committed on
# 2026-06-14 and it sat broken for 432 commits.
#
# Hand-fixing it does not work either: dist/ios/update.js regenerates the file
# unconditionally on every sync, so a corrected copy is overwritten by the next
# run and re-corrupted by the next Windows run. The plugin list is derived from
# what is installed, so committing it also duplicates package.json and drifts.
#
# The runner generates it fresh on macOS, and ios-release.yml fails the build if
# the result contains a backslash or declares fewer plugins than expected.
App/CapApp-SPM/Package.swift
App/CapApp-SPM/Package.resolved
App/CapApp-SPM/symlinks
